<title>USA: Groups suing to block NationsBank acquisition.</title>
<headline>Groups suing to block NationsBank acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Inner City Press/Community on the Move and the New Mexico Alliance said they filed suit in federal appeals court in Denver to reverse the Federal Reserve Board's approval of NationsBank Corp's acquisition of Boatmen's Bancshares Inc.</p>
<p>The groups argued the deal will be anti-competitive and said the board ignored &quot;more than 100 consumer and civil rights lawsuits filed against&quot; NationsCredit, a NationsBank unit, for alleged discriminatory lending practices. A NationsBank spokesman was not immediately available to comment.</p>
</text>
